Subject: [PATCH] clk: qcom: gcc-sm8550: keep the USB GDSCs in retention like sm8650

USB30_PRIM_GDSC and USB3_PHY_GDSC are declared .pwrsts = PWRSTS_OFF_ON, so
genpd powers them off in the noirq phase of a system suspend, the
pm_test=platform test included.  The dwc3 core then skips its re-init
(the glue is a wakeup source), and xhci resumes without power_lost or
XHCI_RESET_ON_RESUME.  RETAIN_FF_ENABLE keeps the flip-flop registers, so
xhci's save/restore handshake appears to succeed on a controller whose
internal context is gone.  Two ways it then fails, both seen on an SM-X910
(blastoise) in USB host role with a hub attached:

 a) the GET_STATUS and stop-endpoint commands time out, 5 s each: "xHCI
    host not responding to stop endpoint command" 11.2 s after the resume
    began, then "HC died" (boots of 2026-11-10 01:33 and 01:43, in the
    boot-time panel recovery cycle);
 b) the controller DMAs from a stale address: "arm-smmu 15000000.iommu:
    Unhandled context fault: fsr=0x402, iova=0x88adc2770, ...,
    cbfrsynra=0x40" and then "xhci-hcd xhci-hcd.2.auto: WARNING: Host
    System Error" (the boot cycle of the saved boot -2, and the real deep
    suspends in host role at 193.6 s and 230.1 s of that boot).

Upstream keeps the same two GDSCs, at the same GDSCR offsets 0x39004 and
0x50018, in retention on sm8650 (commit 8b75c2973997), as on sc8280xp
and x1e80100, and this file's own PCIe GDSCs already got PWRSTS_RET_ON
(967e011013ed); the commit ids are as identified upstream, the shallow
build tree does not carry them.  In this tree gcc-sm8650.c has
PWRSTS_RET_ON for both USB GDSCs, and gcc-sm8550.c for pcie_0_gdsc.

Change only .pwrsts; .flags stays POLL_CFG_GDSCR | RETAIN_FF_ENABLE.  With
PWRSTS_RET_ON, gdsc_disable() leaves the GDSC on (drivers/clk/qcom/gdsc.c,
"If the GDSC supports only a Retention state, apart from ON, leave it in ON
state"); the hardware enters retention when its parent domain goes down.

The SM-X710 builds from the same file, so its USB GDSCs change too: when
its controller runtime-suspends, the GDSC now stays on in software while
genpd still drops the domain's vote on its parent.  Check its idle and
suspend power after the first build with this patch.

Open risk: whether sm8550's USB retention holds through a real CX
collapse in deep suspend.  Validate with (1) one SM-X910 boot with the hub
attached and the boot-cycle USB host park disabled
(/etc/ubuntu-gts9u/usb-host-park-off): no xHCI lines, and the hub's
devices survive the cycle without re-enumerating; then (2) real deep
suspends in host role with the sleep hook's role change disabled the same
way (~/ufs-ice/suspend-cycles.sh on blastoise, hub attached).  Only then
retire ubuntu-gts9u-usb-host-park and the sleep hook's role change.

--- a/drivers/clk/qcom/gcc-sm8550.c
+++ b/drivers/clk/qcom/gcc-sm8550.c
@@ -3058,12 +3058,13 @@
 	.flags = POLL_CFG_GDSCR | RETAIN_FF_ENABLE,
 };
 
+/* Retention across system suspend, as on sm8650: see gcc-sm8550-usb-gdscs-retention.patch */
 static struct gdsc usb30_prim_gdsc = {
 	.gdscr = 0x39004,
 	.pd = {
 		.name = "usb30_prim_gdsc",
 	},
-	.pwrsts = PWRSTS_OFF_ON,
+	.pwrsts = PWRSTS_RET_ON,
 	.flags = POLL_CFG_GDSCR | RETAIN_FF_ENABLE,
 };
 
@@ -3072,7 +3073,7 @@
 	.pd = {
 		.name = "usb3_phy_gdsc",
 	},
-	.pwrsts = PWRSTS_OFF_ON,
+	.pwrsts = PWRSTS_RET_ON,
 	.flags = POLL_CFG_GDSCR | RETAIN_FF_ENABLE,
 };
 
